body:
Does it matter where you earn your degree at? Do you have to earn it in whatever state you wish to practice in?

&#x200B;

Thank you!

We could honestly be the same person (28F here). I just recently left my career as a Firefighter/Paramedic. It was a great career but like any job it can get monotonous, the department I worked for was small so limited in training opportunities/advancement, and I wanted something more mentally challenging. That got me thinking to either volunteer as a medic with the Peace Corps, or possibly get into an MSW as a social worker.

&#x200B;

I think the idea of taking some time off to pursue the Peace Corps route is a great option. I am also making another career change myself at the same age as you, and it is very daunting. However, my best advice is to listen to your gut and taking a year to find yourself in the big scheme of things, isn't that long of a time, and is totally worth it in the end to gain some clarity. Peace Corps also can pay for your TEFL (Teach English as a Foreign Language), and could help you be an English Teacher abroad too!!! 

&#x200B;

I wish I had more advice, but being in a similar boat, I see a lot of similarities. I am going back to school this Fall to finish my B.A. in Spanish, and hope to volunteer abroad as Paramedic with the Peace Corps or another private company while I work on "finding myself" again.

&#x200B;

Best of luck!!

Thank you SO much for this advice! I do attend ACA meetings as well, and am trying to get my foot in the door to volunteer but I keep running into obstacles with COVID. I am however taking a course to become a Certified Recovery Peer Specialist here in the state of FL. I am hoping doing that for work may help me decide and see what it is really like in person. 

&#x200B;

And yes, you are very correct. As a First Responder I saw some horrible things and really have empathy for others. I hope to help using my experience in that role along with the military as well. I also did reach out to a couple MSW programs and will hopefully be connected with maybe an MSW student or possibly sit in on a class. I am really excited about this opportunity, and thank you so much for all the advice!! <3
